* THE ANTILOG PROBE ARGUMENT DECK.  COLUMN 1 IS THE RECORD CODE - A FOR
* AN ARGUMENT, AND ANYTHING ELSE - THIS STAR - FOR A COMMENT THE READ LOOP
* SKIPS.  COLUMN 2 IS THE SIGN, MINUS OR BLANK.  COLUMNS 3 THROUGH 10 ARE
* THE MAGNITUDE, 8 DIGITS AT S EQUALS 7.
*
* THE 100 ARGUMENTS WERE CHOSEN AND NOT SWEPT.  ARG RUNS -9.9999999 TO
* 5.9999999, WHICH IS THE WHOLE OF THE DESIGN RANGE OF 5.6 - THE 8
* POSITION FIELD ITSELF REACHES 9.9999999 - AND THE SET COVERS ALL
* SIXTEEN BIASED DECADES 00 THROUGH 15 AND 51 DISTINCT VALUES OF F1.
*
* 1. TEN EDGE CARDS - THE LOWEST AND THE HIGHEST REPRESENTABLE ARG, THE
*    BIAS ITSELF, AND THE FOUR F1 00 AND F1 99 CORNERS.  THE NEGATIVE
*    ARGUMENTS ARE THE BIAS PATH - WITHOUT THE PLUS 10 THE DECADE SLICE
*    WOULD HAVE TO BE A SIGNED TEST INSTEAD OF A FIELD SLICE.
* 2. SIX HAZARD CARDS.  F FRACTIONAL PART 0.2900000, 0.5700000 AND
*    0.5800000 ARE THE ONLY THREE VALUES OF F, OUT OF TEN MILLION, WHERE
*    A SLICE DONE AS ARITHMETIC DISAGREES WITH A SLICE DONE AS A SLICE.
*    EACH IS PUNCHED AT A NEGATIVE AND AT A POSITIVE ARGUMENT.
* 3. TWENTY TABLE-SWEEP CARDS - F1 00, 05, 10 ... 95, SO THAT NO TENTH
*    OF THE HUNDRED-ENTRY TABLE GOES UNFETCHED.
* 4. THIRTY BAND CARDS - THE THREE ARGUMENTS THE SHOWCASE ITSELF
*    ANTILOGS: MINUS C2 H IN -2.9611 TO 0, MINUS K LOG10 E X IN -1.045
*    TO -0.001, AND LOG10 Q-DOT IN 0.892 TO 3.348 - PLUS THE PRINTED
*    LOG10 RHO RATIO BAND, -2.806 TO 0.152.
* 5. TWELVE RESIDUAL CARDS - R AT 0, AT 1 AND AT 99999, AT F1 00, 50 AND
*    99, AT BOTH SIGNS OF ARG.  R IS FIVE POSITIONS AND 0.0099999 IS THE
*    MOST IT CAN HOLD.
* 6. TWENTY-TWO SWEEP CARDS ACROSS THE WHOLE OF THE RANGE.
*
A-99999999    THE LOWEST ARG - ARGB 0.0000001, DEC 00, F1 00
A-99900000    ARGB 0.0100000 - F1 01
A-90100000    ARGB 0.9900000 - F1 99, R ZERO
A-90000001    ARGB 0.9999999 - F1 99, R AT ITS MAXIMUM
A-90000000    ARGB 1.0000000 - DEC 01, F1 00
A-00000001    ARGB 9.9999999 - DEC 09, F1 99
A 00000000    ARGB 10.0000000 - THE BIAS ITSELF, DEC 10, F1 00
A 00000001    ARGB 10.0000001 - ONE UNIT ABOVE THE BIAS
A 50000000    ARGB 15.0000000 - DEC 15, F1 00
A 59999999    THE HIGHEST ARG - ARGB 15.9999999, DEC 15, F1 99
A-27100000    F IS 0.2900000 - THE FIRST FLOAT-SLICE HAZARD
A-24300000    F IS 0.5700000 - THE SECOND FLOAT-SLICE HAZARD
A-24200000    F IS 0.5800000 - THE THIRD FLOAT-SLICE HAZARD
A 32900000    F IS 0.2900000 - THE HAZARD AT A POSITIVE ARG
A 35700000    F IS 0.5700000 - THE HAZARD AT A POSITIVE ARG
A 35800000    F IS 0.5800000 - THE HAZARD AT A POSITIVE ARG
A-20000000    F1 00 - THE TABLE SWEEP
